  "doc": "Harbour catalogue: harbour types (what a waterfront is furnished with), culture families (which types a culture builds, with weights, its boats, crane and material; `simple`: every port of the family is a plain landing, as a village's) and boat classes (hull plan and rig). A type field `jetties` gives its jetties and finger piers (spacing along the quay, length range for a port of 10 000 people, width, `comb`, `max`), `breakwater` the chance of a breakwater. A family field `yard` is the depth of the port yard behind its quays (34 when absent), which a town wall passes behind. A type field `moles` is the chance that a port of this type keeps the pair of moles of the harbour planner (0 when absent). Read by urban/harbour_furniture.rs (generation) and web/src/render/harbourStyle.ts (2D paint, 3D heights). A culture missing from every family uses `default`. Lengths in metres.",
